			<div class="content" id="post-content-2048438">
									

<p>I vaguely remember some version of the creation myth stating that the gods all picked what they wanted to rule over, and Hades either lost a game of chance or picked the Underworld himself because it was quiet. Either way, I figure that since he's the older brother and all, he's the type to be &quot;sorry guys, gotta balance the books of the dead&quot; when Zeus and Poseidon are all &quot;HEY BRO LET'S GO PARTAY&quot;.</p>
<p>Disney Hades is hilarious with his fire hair and smooth talking, but I didn't really like that he wanted to take over Olympus. If anything, Hades tried to avoid getting involved with the problems all the other deities had/made/ended up in.</p>

